  },
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "In 1916, two girls of {wealthy} families, best friends from Auburn, N.Y.—Dorothy Woodruff and Rosamond Underwood—traveled to a {settlement} in the {Rocky Mountains} to teach in a {remote} one-room {schoolhouse} with only a {blackboard} and some basic supplies.While most of their peers ( (同龄人) ) chose to {marry} or engage in dull social activities, the two women embarked on a journey that would take them far from the {parties} , fine {silk} clothing and the {buffets} they were used to, leaving behind the {estate} of their rich families.So for them to move to Elkhead, Colorado, to {instruct} the children, {whose shoes} were held together with {string} , was a surprise.The mountains of Colorado, {dotted} with {mines} and wandering {goats} , were a stark ( (鲜明的) ) contrast to their daily life.Their stay in Elkhead is the subject of Nothing Daunted : The Unexpected Education of Two Society Girls in the West, by Dorothy Wickenden-a magazine editor and Dorothy Woodruff's {granddaughter} .",
      "cn": "1916年，来自纽约州奥本市的两位 富 家千金——多萝西·伍德拉夫和罗莎蒙德·安德伍德，这对挚友一同前往 落基山脉 的一个 定居点 ，在一所 偏远的 单间 校舍 里教书，那里只有一块 黑板 和一些基本的教具。当时，她们的大多数同龄人都选择 结婚 ，或参加无聊的社交活动，而这两位女性却开启了一段旅程，远离了她们习以为常的 聚会 、精致的 丝绸 服饰和 自助餐 ，离开了自家的豪 宅 。她们搬到科罗拉多州的埃尔克黑德，去 教 那些 鞋子 要用 绳子 绑到一起的孩子们，这一举动令人惊讶。科罗拉多州的山脉上 布满 了 矿场 ，还有四处游荡的 山羊 ，与她们的日常生活形成了鲜明的对比。她们在埃尔克黑德的这段经历，正是多萝西·威肯登——一位杂志编辑，也是多萝西·伍德拉夫的 孙女 ——所著的《无所 畏惧 ：两位上流社会女孩在西部的 意外 历练》一书的主题。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "Why did they go then? Well, they wanted to do something useful.Soon, however, they realized what they had {undertaken} .",
      "cn": "那么，她们为什么要去西部呢？好吧，是因为她们想做点有用的事。不过，她们很快就意识到了自己 肩负 的任务。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "They moved in with a local family, the Harrisons, and, like them, had little {privacy} , rare {baths} , and a blanket of snow on their {quilt} when they {woke} up in the morning—harsh conditions that would make most society men or women {quit} .Some mornings, Rosamond and Dorothy would arrive at the schoolhouse to find the children {weeping} from the cold.In spring, the snow was replaced by {mud} over ice.One can imagine them learning to {sew} their own clothes, and perhaps {mending} their students’ {torn shirts} and {shorts} .They wrote letters home, sharing their experiences with their families and {brothers} back east.They never showed {pity} , instead embracing their new life with {determination} .",
      "cn": "她们住进了当地的哈里森家，和这家人一样，几乎没有 隐私 ，很少 洗澡 ，早上 醒来 时 被子 上盖着一层薄雪。这样恶劣的条件会让大多数上流社会男女 放弃 。有些早晨，罗莎蒙德和多萝西赶到校舍，只见孩子们冻得直 哭 。春天，积雪会被冰上的 泥泞 取代。可以想象，她们学着 缝制 自己的衣服，也许还会 修补 学生 破洞的衬衫 和 短裤 。她们写信回家，与留在东部的家人和 兄弟 分享她们的经历。她们毫无自 怜 之意，而是 坚定 地拥抱新的生活。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "In Wickenden's book, she expanded on the history of the West and also on {feminism} , as it was uncommon for young {educated} women to step beyond the traditional roles of {wives} and mothers.Her book lets readers {witness} the frontier life of the early 20th century.A {hair-raising section} concerns the building of the {railroads} , which entailed ( (牵涉) ) {drilling} through the Rockies, often in {blinding snowstorms} .The book ends with Rosamond and Dorothy's return to Auburn.",
      "cn": "威肯登在书中补充了美国西部的历史和 女权主义 相关的内容，因为在当时， 受过教育的 年轻女性鲜少能够突破 妻子 、母亲等传统角色。她的书让读者 见证 了20世纪初的边疆生活。书中有一 段惊心动魄的 描写讲述了修建 铁路 的过程：工人们常常要冒着 让人视线模糊 的暴风雪 在落基山脉 开凿 隧道。这本书以罗莎蒙德和多萝西回到奥本市结束。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "Wickenden is a very good {storyteller} .The {sweep} of the {land} and the stoicism ( (坚忍) ) of the people move her to some beautiful writing.Here is a picture of Dorothy Woodruff, on her {horse} , looking down from a hill top:“When the sun slipped behind the mountains, it {shed} a rosy {glow} all around them.Then a full {moon} rose.The snow was marked only by small animals: foxes, coyotes, {mice} , and {varying} hares, which turned white in the winter.”",
      "cn": "威肯登是一位很好的 讲述者 。这片 广阔 的 土地 和人们的坚忍不拔驱使她创作出了优美的篇章。她描写了这样一幅画面：多萝西·伍德拉夫骑在 马 上，从山顶俯瞰——“当太阳滑落到山后，在周围 洒下 了玫瑰色的 光 ；然后，一轮满 月 升起。雪地上只有小动物留下的足迹——狐狸、郊狼、 老鼠 ，还有随冬季换上白毛的 变色 野兔。” 5NoOncib/NjiX02BpMIzP4m+378Hw1xTRxUdPaP/PFjKUFq4K2G7tp6ZLYoCE601yW1W39VMdLmovFdSHs4nVQ=="
    }
  ],
